  "equipment_type": "Fan coil room controller",
  "applies_to": "Regin RCF 230 V wall-mounted fan coil controllers with built-in communication (models with a C in the name).",
  "summary": "The RCF is a wall-mounted fan coil controller for heating, cooling and change-over with a three-speed or EC fan. Models with a C in the name have an RS485 port that runs EXOline, Modbus or BACnet MS/TP; BACnet is selected with parameter 57. All communicating models share one object list; objects for functions a model lacks stay unused.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "1.4-1-00 or later (BTL listed from 1.2-1-00)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object list from chapter 19 of the RCF manual (rev 3.2, May 2021), pages 52-56.",
    "Rows printed as 'Not used in this model' (AV 7-8, AV 11, AV 17-26, BI 1, BI 4-6, BV 0, BV 5-6, BV 8, MI 0, MV 3) are left out. BV 11 is not listed at all.",
    "Value objects are not commandable (no priority array).",
    "RegioMinECFanSpeed and RegioMaxFanSpeed (AV 27-28) only apply to the RCF-230CTD-EC.",
    "EDE files for the BACnet objects come with the Regio tool installation."
  ],
